Subject: [PATCH] wifi: uwe5622: supply the AP channel in the firmware beacon

The START_AP command carries a beacon template but no separate channel.
Hostapd omits the DS Parameter Set on 5 GHz. The firmware used by the
Orange Pi Zero 3 rejects these requests with NOT_SUPPORT_ERROR even when
the HT Operation element contains the correct primary channel.

Supply a missing DS Parameter Set in the command template using the
requested channel, or the valid driver channel override. The head buffer
already reserves 32 extra bytes. Keep existing DS elements unchanged.
This makes channel 36 AP startup succeed and restores visibility on an
independent Intel AX200 receiver.

--- a/unisocwifi/cfg80211.c
+++ b/unisocwifi/cfg80211.c
@@ -1019,6 +1019,16 @@ static int sprdwl_cfg80211_start_ap(stru
 		tail_len = beacon->tail_len;
 	}
 
+	/* Firmware requires a DS channel even for 5 GHz AP startup. */
+	if (!cfg80211_find_ie(WLAN_EID_DS_PARAMS,
+			head + offsetof(struct ieee80211_mgmt, u.beacon.variable),
+			head_len - offsetof(struct ieee80211_mgmt, u.beacon.variable))) {
+		head[head_len++] = WLAN_EID_DS_PARAMS;
+		head[head_len++] = 1;
+		head[head_len++] = is_valid_channel(wiphy, chn) ? chn :
+			ieee80211_frequency_to_channel(settings->chandef.chan->center_freq);
+	}
+
 	sprdwl_change_beacon(vif, beacon);
 
 	if (!beacon->head) {
